{
  "sn1.35:0.1": "Linked Discourses 1.35 ",
  "sn1.35:0.2": "4. The Host of a Hundred Felicities ",
  "sn1.35:0.3": "Fault-Finding Deities ",
  "sn1.35:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "sn1.35:1.2": "Then, late at night, several glorious deities of the host of the fault-finders, lighting up the entire Jeta’s Grove, went up to the Buddha, and stood in the air. ",
  "sn1.35:1.3": "Standing in the air, one deity spoke this verse in the Buddha’s presence: ",
  "sn1.35:2.1": "“Someone who pretends ",
  "sn1.35:2.2": "to be other than they really are, ",
  "sn1.35:2.3": "is like a cheating gambler ",
  "sn1.35:2.4": "who enjoys what was gained by theft. ",
  "sn1.35:3.1": "You should only say what you would do; ",
  "sn1.35:3.2": "you shouldn’t say what you wouldn’t do. ",
  "sn1.35:3.3": "The wise will recognize ",
  "sn1.35:3.4": "one who talks without doing.” ",
  "sn1.35:4.1": "“Not just by speaking, ",
  "sn1.35:4.2": "nor solely by listening, ",
  "sn1.35:4.3": "are you able to progress ",
  "sn1.35:4.4": "on this hard path, ",
  "sn1.35:4.5": "by which the attentive practicing absorption ",
  "sn1.35:4.6": "are released from Māra’s bonds. ",
  "sn1.35:5.1": "The attentive certainly don’t act like that, ",
  "sn1.35:5.2": "for they understand the way of the world. ",
  "sn1.35:5.3": "The attentive are quenched by understanding, ",
  "sn1.35:5.4": "they’ve crossed over clinging to the world.” ",
  "sn1.35:6